msgid ""
"<strong>A)\n"
"                                    OFFER</strong><br/> 1. All the designs and / or sketches that\n"
"                                    could accompany our offers are indicative and once the offer is\n"
"                                    accepted, our company puts at your disposal our technical\n"
"                                    department for any kind of doubt, consultation, clarification\n"
"                                    that you wish to request. In the future our company will be\n"
"                                    named as ATECA. 2. Unless otherwise agreed, the validity of the\n"
"                                    ATECA offer is 30 calendar days. 3. Once this offer is accepted,\n"
"                                    it will be valid during the year of its issuance. 4. ATECA\n"
"                                    offers will be subject to acceptance. The acceptance of the\n"
"                                    offer will result in the initiation of a contractual\n"
"                                    relationship between <br/><strong>B)\n"
"                                        MATERIALS</strong><br/> 1. The contracted material has been\n"
"                                    previously chosen by the client at his convenience, who states\n"
"                                    that he considers it suitable for the intended use 2. The\n"
"                                    materials that are supplied for rent are property of ATECA, who\n"
"                                    reserves the domain of them at all times. The assignment,\n"
"                                    sublease or subrogation of the material in favor of third\n"
"                                    parties is prohibited. The client becomes custodian of the\n"
"                                    materials supplied from its arrival until its withdrawal by\n"
"                                    ATECA. The client becomes custodian of the materials supplied\n"
"                                    from their arrival until their withdrawal. It is totally\n"
"                                    forbidden to assign or sublet the supplied materials, as well as\n"
"                                    to transfer them to another work different from the one\n"
"                                    specified in this contract. The customer will be responsible for\n"
"                                    the supervision of the materials on the site, in terms of theft,\n"
"                                    bad treatment, improper use, etc. In case of loss, deterioration\n"
"                                    or theft of the material, it will be invoiced at the prices in\n"
"                                    force in the general rate of ATECA, which is in force at the\n"
"                                    time of the withdrawal of the material. The materials supplied\n"
"                                    will be kept by the customer with the due diligence of\n"
"                                    maintenance until their return, committing to deliver them in\n"
"                                    the state in which they were received, responding in any case\n"
"                                    the client regarding irreparable damages due to blows, crushing,\n"
"                                    etc. or due to paint, cement, welding or rust. 3. Under the\n"
"                                    regime of sale of material, the transfer of the property of the\n"
"                                    merchandise will not occur until the full payment of the sale\n"
"                                    that appears in the contract or offer accepted, since ATECA\n"
"                                    reserves the domain of the merchandise supplied. For them the\n"
"                                    sale is understood subject to suspensive condition. The place of\n"
"                                    fulfillment of the contract is established in GRAN CANARIAS, in\n"
"                                    the offices of ATECA., So any payment must be made in the\n"
"                                    offices of ATECA in Gran Canarias and in the manner established\n"
"                                    in the contract or offer accepted. 4. In the event that parts\n"
"                                    other than those offered are supplied, either by modifications\n"
"                                    or improvements in them, the elements actually supplied will be\n"
"                                    invoiced at the current price, and the appropriate contract or\n"
"                                    new acceptance of offer must be subscribed according to the new\n"
"                                    materials effectively supplied, with full indemnity for ATECA <br/><strong>C)\n"
"                                    PRECIOS</strong><br/> 1. All prices must be considered net, by\n"
"                                    which they must be increased with the IGIC applied at all times\n"
"                                    2. If, from the existence of the contractual relationship, up to\n"
"                                    the delivery of the material, more than 90 calendar days, for\n"
"                                    causes totally unrelated to ATECA, the price will be revised and\n"
"                                    updated in accordance with the price list in force at the date\n"
"                                    of delivery. <br/><strong>D) TRANSPORT</strong><br/> 1. The\n"
"                                    client will indicate the place where the materials will be\n"
"                                    supplied, being of his responsibility all the actions that may\n"
"                                    derive from the place in which they are deposited, for the\n"
"                                    damages that could cause them. 2. At the time of arrival of the\n"
"                                    goods to the destination set by the customer, there must be\n"
"                                    someone with sufficient powers of the client who can carry out\n"
"                                    the receipt and sign the corresponding delivery notes. In the\n"
"                                    event that no responsible or authorized person is present, the\n"
"                                    parties expressly accept that the signature of the transporter\n"
"                                    who makes the delivery will be sufficient for the merchandise\n"
"                                    reflected in the delivery note to be understood as received. 3.\n"
"                                    If the stockpile is more than 20m away from the pit, and has\n"
"                                    been manually loaded, the corresponding transport will be\n"
"                                    charged for <br/><strong>E) SUPPLY, SPACES AND\n"
"                                        STOCKPILES</strong><br/> 1. The customer will specify the\n"
"                                    place where they will be supplied and installed, where\n"
"                                    appropriate, the materials, being their responsibility all\n"
"                                    actions that may derive from the place where they are deposited\n"
"                                    or installed, for any damage they may cause. 2. The client will\n"
"                                    be responsible for the provision of the space required for\n"
"                                    loading and unloading, as well as a storage area for the\n"
"                                    material at the foot of the pit, having previously prepared the\n"
"                                    corresponding permits or licenses and even the protection fences\n"
"                                    if necessary. 3. The electrical supply, water, lifting of\n"
"                                    materials with crane or other means of elevation and in general,\n"
"                                    any general need for the assembly and disassembly of\n"
"                                    scaffolding, will be at the customer's expense <br/><strong>F)\n"
"                                    RENTALS</strong><br/> 1. With the provision of labor for hire\n"
"                                    by ATECA, the rents will be accrued daily, from the start date\n"
"                                    of the assembly until the completion of the dismantling, with a\n"
"                                    minimum billing of 15 days. 2. With labor on behalf of the\n"
"                                    client, the rents will accrue daily, from the date of departure\n"
"                                    of the ULMA warehouse until the date of return to them, with a\n"
"                                    minimum of 15 days invoicing <br/><strong>G) LABOR</strong><br/>\n"
"                                    1. Stop times not attributable to ATECA (inability to access\n"
"                                    work, adverse weather conditions, obstacles or other trades\n"
"                                    interfering in the pit, lack of electricity supply, lack of\n"
"                                    minimum safety conditions, stop for safety reasons etc.) will be\n"
"                                    billed by administration. 2. The work to be done with pipe and\n"
"                                    clamp, as well as modifications and revisions of scaffolds\n"
"                                    already installed, will be billed by administration. 3. It will\n"
"                                    be for the client's account the adequacy of the implantation\n"
"                                    area or any other previous operation that was necessary. 4. It\n"
"                                    will be the customer's responsibility to keep the pit clean and\n"
"                                    clear of other trades so that the haulage and assembly and\n"
"                                    disassembly work can be carried out 5. Will be on behalf of the\n"
"                                    client how many building permits, taxes, fees, permits for\n"
"                                    occupation of sidewalk and roadway; facultative directions etc.\n"
"                                    are necessary for the installation of contracted scaffolding <br/><strong>H)\n"
"                                    ADVERTISING</strong><br/> 1. ATECA reserves the right placement\n"
"                                    of own publicity or third in their scaffolding, not being able\n"
"                                    to place some advertising without express authorization. Purpose\n"
"                                    publication in advertising media of any kind limited period of\n"
"                                    time and in any country in the world and their transfer to third\n"
"                                    parties. <br/><strong>P)\n"
"                                        CONTENCIUS CLAUSES</strong><br/> 1. Failure to comply with\n"
"                                    these General Conditions and, in particular, the form, deadline\n"
"                                    or conditions of payment established in the attached offer\n"
"                                    accepted, will be sufficient reasons to terminate this contract,\n"
"                                    and ATECA will be able to dispose of its materials without prior\n"
"                                    request to the client, and without prejudice to any subsequent\n"
"                                    claims that may arise; so with the signing of the contract or\n"
"                                    offer is authorized by the client to ATECA at the entrance to\n"
"                                    the place where the scaffolds are located and proceed to its\n"
"                                    disassembly and removal, but may choose ATECA not to perform the\n"
"                                    dismantling of materials or scaffolding until the customer is\n"
"                                    aware of their payment obligations. In this case, and until its\n"
"                                    cash payment, will continue accruing to ATECA all the concepts\n"
"                                    and prices provided in the contract or offer accepted, with the\n"
"                                    corresponding legal interests of delay, increasing billing\n"
"                                    accordingly until full payment or settlement 2. Likewise, ATECA\n"
"                                    will have the right to be indemnified by the client, for all\n"
"                                    those damages and losses of any kind that, as a consequence of\n"
"                                    the contractual breach of this, they had irrigated. 3. If the\n"
"                                    client decides under his exclusive responsibility and with full\n"
"                                    indemnity for ATECA, perform at his sole account and charge,\n"
"                                    dismantling, loading and unloading, and delivery to the ULMA\n"
"                                    stores of the contracted materials, ATECA will be bound to his\n"
"                                    receipt provided that at the same time the delivery is made\n"
"                                    effective by that established in the contract or offer accepted\n"
"                                    and in accordance with the general conditions, must be\n"
"                                    subscribed, if there is agreement between the parties, document\n"
"                                    or record of receipt, signed and dated in accordance with both\n"
"                                    parties 4. In the event that any condition was or became invalid\n"
"                                    or unacceptable, it will not affect the validity of the other\n"
"                                    conditions."
